<title>GERMANY: Pan-German May industry output falls 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Pan-German May industry output falls 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  May 97     Apr 97	May 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -0.2	 +0.3	 +1.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.5	 +3.0	 -1.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		100.6	100.8	99.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously announced data in parentheses.</p>
<p>The ministry noted that April data had been revised upwards and announced that May data were likely to be revised downward.</p>
<p>&quot;Because there are considerably fewer working days in May than in April, on the other hand we have to expect that the latest data later will be revised downwards,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    May 97		   Apr 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			 74.3     -6.1	79.1     +10.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    100.4     +0.5	99.9	+0.2</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods    106.3     +1.1     105.1	+1.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods	 98.3     -1.1	99.4	+2.7</p>
<p>	Consumer durables   83.1     -3.9	86.5	-9.9</p>
<p>	Consumer goods	99.6     +5.1	94.8	-3.3</p>
<p> Energy output	     106.3     +0.9     105.3	+2.5</p>
<p> Construction		106.6     -5.4     112.7	-1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr/May 1997 with Feb/Mar 1997:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  +0.5</p>
<p> Construction			    -4.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.0</p>
<p> Mining				    +6.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   +4.0</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 -2.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +2.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-May 97 with Apr-May 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +2.5</p>
<p> Mining				    +0.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +4.4</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   +7.2</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +4.6</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +0.7</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -1.2</p>
<p> Energy output			   -1.1</p>
<p> Construction			    -8.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
